cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the repository version and preserve the source-data citations recorded by each analysis or case study."
type: software
title: "Materials Characterization Analyzer"
authors:
  - name: "jhin0410-lgtm"
version: 0.11.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/jhin0410-lgtm/materials-characterization-analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/jhin0410-lgtm/materials-characterization-analyzer"
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  A provenance-aware Python command-line toolkit for cautious baseline analysis,
  checksum-bound public real-data case studies, fail-closed validation contracts,
  and reproducible output generation across XRD, SEM, EDS, Raman, TEM, SAED, XPS,
  FTIR, TGA, and DSC characterization workflows. The software separates software
  validation from scientific validation and does not automatically confirm phases,
  compounds, chemical states, functional groups, reactions, mechanisms,
  quantitative composition, segmentation validity, crystallographic correctness,
  raw-image identity, acquisition independence, pixel calibration, or physical
  particle dimensions.
keywords:
  - materials science
  - materials characterization
  - provenance
  - XRD
  - SEM
  - EDS
  - Raman
  - TEM
  - SAED
  - XPS
  - FTIR
  - TGA
  - DSC
